{{also|infusé}}
==English==

===Etymology===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*ǵʰewd-}}
From {{inh|en|enm|infusen}}, from {{der|en|la|infusus}}, from {{m|la|infundo}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ɪnˈfjuz/}}
* {{audio|en|En-us-infuse.ogg|Audio (US)}}
* {{rhymes|en|uːz|s=2}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# {{lb|en|transitive}} To cause to become an [[element]] of something; to [[insert]] or [[fill]].
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[steep]] in a liquid, so as to [[extract]] the soluble [[constituent]]s (usually [[medicinal]] or [[herbal]]).
#* {{RQ:Coxe The American Dispensary}}
#*: One scruple of the dried leaves is '''infused''' in ten ounces of warm water.
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To inspire; to inspirit or animate; to fill (with).
#*{{RQ:Shakespeare Henry 6-3|V|iv|passage='''Infuse''' his breast with magnanimity.}}
#*{{RQ:Shakespeare Richard 2|III|ii|passage='''infusing''' him with self and vain conceit}}
#* {{RQ:Landon Duty|page=219|volume=II|passage=The uproar of the sea, the yell of the Indians, the rapidity with which the boat at intervals was driven, threatening at every moment to be engulphed, might have '''infused''' terror into the most undaunted;{{...}}}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[instill]] as a quality.
#*{{RQ:Shakespeare Merchant of Venice|IV|i|passage=That souls of animals '''infuse''' themselves <br> Into the trunks of men.}}
#* {{RQ:Swift An Essay on Modern Education}}
#*: Why should he desire to have qualities '''infused''' into his son, which himself never possessed, or knew, or found the want of, in the acquisition of his wealth?
# {{lb|en|intransitive}} To undergo [[infusion]].
#: {{ux|en|Let it '''infuse''' for five minutes.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To make an infusion with (an ingredient); to [[tincture]]; to [[saturate]].
#* {{RQ:Bacon Sylva Sylvarum|passage=if you '''infuse''' Rubarb for an hour ; and crush it well, it will purge better, and bind the Body less after the purġing, than if it stood Twenty four hours}}
# {{lb|en|transitive|obsolete}} To pour in, as a liquid; to pour (into or upon); to shed.
#* {{RQ:Denham The Progress of Learning}}
#*: That strong Circean liquor cease t’'''infuse'''.

